Commands to show in the interview

Open another terminal:

cd ~/tiny_slam_ros2_ws
source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
source install/setup.bash

Show the node:

ros2 node list

Show the topics:

ros2 topic list

Show everything connected to the node:

ros2 node info /tiny_slam_node

Show the live SLAM status:

ros2 topic echo /tiny_slam/status

It should display changing values such as:

data: 'step=75/216 odom_rmse=0.182m slam_rmse=0.164m'

Show the LiDAR publication frequency:

ros2 topic hz /scan

Inspect one odometry message:

ros2 topic echo /odom --once

Inspect the map metadata:

ros2 topic echo /map --once

Reset the simulation through a ROS service:

ros2 service call /tiny_slam/reset \
std_srvs/srv/Trigger "{}"
